  "response_text": "The stack pool is a reserved section of memory used to hold the stacks for all threads created by the OS. Each thread needs its own stack space to store local variables, function call information, and CPU state during context switches. In future labs, we\u2019ll use the stack pool to allocate a separate stack for each thread. This allows multiple threads to run \"concurrently\" (in a time-sliced manner) without interfering with each other\u2019s data, because each one operates in its own section of the stack pool.\\n",
